#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/core/README.md:4
msgid ""
"C11 caller-owned request admission, stable control identities, completion "
"state and monotonic absolute deadlines. No devices, OS scheduler, allocation"
" or global registry. Public interfaces are in `include/nexus/core`."
msgstr ""
"C11 caller-owned request admission, stable control identities, completion "
"state and monotonic absolute deadlines. No devices, OS scheduler, allocation"
" or global registry. Public interfaces are in `include/nexus/core`."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/core/README.md:8
msgid ""
"REJECTED retains no references. An accepted chain borrows request and "
"buffers until acquire-observed SETTLED. SETTLED is its last request access. "
"Cancel/timeouts never revoke a borrow; failed drain keeps QUARANTINED "
"storage alive. Producers wait on latched state; a single executor services "
"the operation. Queue adapters own their outer request and use explicit inner"
" provider metadata where needed."
msgstr ""
"REJECTED retains no references. An accepted chain borrows request and "
"buffers until acquire-observed SETTLED. SETTLED is its last request access. "
"Cancel/timeouts never revoke a borrow; failed drain keeps QUARANTINED "
"storage alive. Producers wait on latched state; a single executor services "
"the operation. Queue adapters own their outer request and use explicit inner"
" provider metadata where needed."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/core/README.md:14
msgid ""
"`tests/contracts/core_contract_test.c` executes publication, admission, "
"wrapping time arithmetic and terminal-state invariants. Host results do not "
"prove MCU interrupt ordering or worst-case execution time."
msgstr ""
"`tests/contracts/core_contract_test.c` executes publication, admission, "
"wrapping time arithmetic and terminal-state invariants. Host results do not "
"prove MCU interrupt ordering or worst-case execution time."

msgid "Admission, shutdown and reuse"
msgstr "Admission, shutdown and reuse"

msgid "Initialize fresh, unpublished storage once. `nx_request_prepare` resets only a READY request or a consumed SETTLED incarnation. It cannot discover outstanding adapter loans, control commands or observers; the owning adapter must join them. One serialized executor admits and advances the request. The request state is a release/acquire predicate, independent of whether a notification was delivered."
msgstr "Initialize fresh, unpublished storage once. `nx_request_prepare` resets only a READY request or a consumed SETTLED incarnation. It cannot discover outstanding adapter loans, control commands or observers; the owning adapter must join them. One serialized executor admits and advances the request. The request state is a release/acquire predicate, independent of whether a notification was delivered."

msgid "The complete shutdown order is:"
msgstr "The complete shutdown order is:"

msgid "Close admission and stop new controls or observation bindings."
msgstr "Close admission and stop new controls or observation bindings."

msgid "Let the unique executor cancel and drain hardware, IRQ, DMA and deferred references. A failed drain retains the request and payload in QUARANTINED; neither a timeout nor detaching an observer authorizes reclamation."
msgstr "Let the unique executor cancel and drain hardware, IRQ, DMA and deferred references. A failed drain retains the request and payload in QUARANTINED; neither a timeout nor detaching an observer authorizes reclamation."

msgid "Before release-publishing SETTLED, detach every provider reference and capture any independently lived wake target. Settlement is the provider's final request/payload access. A pending notification must not retain the request."
msgstr "Before release-publishing SETTLED, detach every provider reference and capture any independently lived wake target. Settlement is the provider's final request/payload access. A pending notification must not retain the request."

msgid "Acquire-observe SETTLED and consume its result. Separately acknowledge queued controls and join all task, diagnostic and completion observers, including already executing calls. Detach their sidecars under the adapter's guard."
msgstr "Acquire-observe SETTLED and consume its result. Separately acknowledge queued controls and join all task, diagnostic and completion observers, including already executing calls. Detach their sidecars under the adapter's guard."

msgid "Release the stable slot. Only then prepare/rebind the request, reclaim its storage, or stop dependencies once every other consumer has joined."
msgstr "Release the stable slot. Only then prepare/rebind the request, reclaim its storage, or stop dependencies once every other consumer has joined."

msgid "The adapter synchronizes bind, lookup and release. Epochs identify incarnations inside one stable slot's lifetime; they are not globally unique wire IDs. `UINT64_MAX` is the last usable epoch. Its next bind rejects without changing the slot or output. Retire that exhausted slot; never zero it while any old command can address its storage. Replacing storage or restarting the owner requires joining all controls/observers and withdrawing every old reference first."
msgstr "The adapter synchronizes bind, lookup and release. Epochs identify incarnations inside one stable slot's lifetime; they are not globally unique wire IDs. `UINT64_MAX` is the last usable epoch. Its next bind rejects without changing the slot or output. Retire that exhausted slot; never zero it while any old command can address its storage. Replacing storage or restarting the owner requires joining all controls/observers and withdrawing every old reference first."

msgid "The maintained UART/SPI example in [`io_owner_diagnostic_pipeline_test.cpp`](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tests/google/io_owner_diagnostic_pipeline_test.cpp) uses real Native providers and owner adapters: failed drain retains the hardware, recovery settles, observers detach, and only then does provider stop succeed. `core_lifecycle_test.cpp` additionally checks the full legal-transition matrix, prepare rejection and the last usable epoch. The publication regression in the C contract target observes results across real host threads without a wake hint. None of these tests authorizes concurrent admissions or unguarded slot access."
msgstr "The maintained UART/SPI example in [`io_owner_diagnostic_pipeline_test.cpp`](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tests/google/io_owner_diagnostic_pipeline_test.cpp) uses real Native providers and owner adapters: failed drain retains the hardware, recovery settles, observers detach, and only then does provider stop succeed. `core_lifecycle_test.cpp` additionally checks the full legal-transition matrix, prepare rejection and the last usable epoch. The publication regression in the C contract target observes results across real host threads without a wake hint. None of these tests authorizes concurrent admissions or unguarded slot access."

msgid "Clock domains and bounded waits"
msgstr "Clock domains and bounded waits"

msgid "A `nx_clock32_t` has one execution owner, a stable nonzero frequency and an uninterrupted counter. Its maximum observation gap is strictly less than `2^32 / frequency_hz` seconds: at 1 MHz this is 4294.967296 seconds. Equal snapshots after a full wrap are indistinguishable from no progress. Account for idle, masked work, Flash maintenance, sleep and worst-case owner latency; this helper cannot detect a missed wrap. A successful observation commits the tick extension and output together. Invalid arguments, alias or exhaustion change neither. Output storage must be distinct from the complete extension state."
msgstr "A `nx_clock32_t` has one execution owner, a stable nonzero frequency and an uninterrupted counter. Its maximum observation gap is strictly less than `2^32 / frequency_hz` seconds: at 1 MHz this is 4294.967296 seconds. Equal snapshots after a full wrap are indistinguishable from no progress. Account for idle, masked work, Flash maintenance, sleep and worst-case owner latency; this helper cannot detect a missed wrap. A successful observation commits the tick extension and output together. Invalid arguments, alias or exhaustion change neither. Output storage must be distinct from the complete extension state."

msgid "The selected physical clock has its own reviewed overflow/service contract; the generic 32-bit helper does not establish that provider's readiness. Stop, restart, clock replacement or frequency change creates a new domain. Join all deadline consumers before withdrawing the old clock; even an equal numerical timestamp cannot make old deadlines valid. This is a lifecycle rule, without a mandatory generation field in each request. A terminal clock failure retains loans and follows the selected provider's fail-stop contract."
msgstr "The selected physical clock has its own reviewed overflow/service contract; the generic 32-bit helper does not establish that provider's readiness. Stop, restart, clock replacement or frequency change creates a new domain. Join all deadline consumers before withdrawing the old clock; even an equal numerical timestamp cannot make old deadlines valid. This is a lifecycle rule, without a mandatory generation field in each request. A terminal clock failure retains loans and follows the selected provider's fail-stop contract."

msgid "For a required finite wait, use `nx_deadline_finite_after(now, duration, &end)` before admission and handle failure. It rejects the nonfinite `now` sentinel and any sum reaching the sentinel without rewriting `end`; zero duration is valid. `nx_deadline_after` keeps its explicit saturation-to-infinite-wait semantics. Neither helper reads a clock or proves readiness; a zero clock value is not a startup acknowledgement."
msgstr "For a required finite wait, use `nx_deadline_finite_after(now, duration, &end)` before admission and handle failure. It rejects the nonfinite `now` sentinel and any sum reaching the sentinel without rewriting `end`; zero duration is valid. `nx_deadline_after` keeps its explicit saturation-to-infinite-wait semantics. Neither helper reads a clock or proves readiness; a zero clock value is not a startup acknowledgement."

msgid "Optional observation and minimal fault capture"
msgstr "Optional observation and minimal fault capture"

msgid "Request observation is a copied diagnostic view, not another execution owner. Its gaps and transition counts describe sampled observations, not IRQ latency, WCET or every intervening state. The stable slot outlives the observer; the caller serializes sampling against request reuse and slot release. The helper rejects output overlap with known control objects. Only the caller knows full request, payload and external context spans and must keep them disjoint and alive."
msgstr "Request observation is a copied diagnostic view, not another execution owner. Its gaps and transition counts describe sampled observations, not IRQ latency, WCET or every intervening state. The stable slot outlives the observer; the caller serializes sampling against request reuse and slot release. The helper rejects output overlap with known control objects. Only the caller knows full request, payload and external context spans and must keep them disjoint and alive."

msgid "The weak `nx_fault_observe` remains stateless. A product can link one bounded C11 override writing an explicitly owned, debugger-visible record. The following minimal shape deliberately stores no clock, task name or dynamic pointer:"
msgstr "The weak `nx_fault_observe` remains stateless. A product can link one bounded C11 override writing an explicitly owned, debugger-visible record. The following minimal shape deliberately stores no clock, task name or dynamic pointer:"

msgid "This is best-effort forensic storage inspected after terminal halt, with no coherent concurrent-reader or nested-fault guarantee. `volatile` is not a lock or a release/acquire protocol. The owning product selects valid writable memory and retention requirements. The hook cannot repair a corrupt stack, claim safe outputs, release loans or rely on a clock, kernel or transport. It never changes incoming masks. If it returns, the reporting terminal path still parks. The existing FreeRTOS fail-stop tests exercise this actual hook boundary, retained requests and preservation of PRIMASK/BASEPRI/FAULTMASK. No snapshot, queue, worker or record is added to the default Core image."
msgstr "This is best-effort forensic storage inspected after terminal halt, with no coherent concurrent-reader or nested-fault guarantee. `volatile` is not a lock or a release/acquire protocol. The owning product selects valid writable memory and retention requirements. The hook cannot repair a corrupt stack, claim safe outputs, release loans or rely on a clock, kernel or transport. It never changes incoming masks. If it returns, the reporting terminal path still parks. The existing FreeRTOS fail-stop tests exercise this actual hook boundary, retained requests and preservation of PRIMASK/BASEPRI/FAULTMASK. No snapshot, queue, worker or record is added to the default Core image."

msgid "Stack and explicitly placed memory"
msgstr "Stack and explicitly placed memory"

msgid "For `nx_stack_observe`, the caller first acquires an external quiescent lease: the stack owner is stopped/joined and cannot execute or receive an exception on the sampled stack while the read is in progress. Supply the original painted low-address region, excluding active frames, current SP and independently sized exception/context reservation. Boot startup establishes MSP paint provenance; the helper does not infer it. Never paint a live stack or mask interrupts around an unbounded scan. Cost is bounded by the declared byte count; reservations or writes equal to the paint hide use, so the result is not a proven stack peak. `tests/google/stack_observation_test.cpp` checks bounds, read-only behavior and alias rejection; OS stack-snapshot helpers own the separate task-context rules."
msgstr "For `nx_stack_observe`, the caller first acquires an external quiescent lease: the stack owner is stopped/joined and cannot execute or receive an exception on the sampled stack while the read is in progress. Supply the original painted low-address region, excluding active frames, current SP and independently sized exception/context reservation. Boot startup establishes MSP paint provenance; the helper does not infer it. Never paint a live stack or mask interrupts around an unbounded scan. Cost is bounded by the declared byte count; reservations or writes equal to the paint hide use, so the result is not a proven stack peak. `tests/google/stack_observation_test.cpp` checks bounds, read-only behavior and alias rejection; OS stack-snapshot helpers own the separate task-context rules."

