msgid "Physical Platform builds compile the selected controller domains and authored component dependencies from the CMake source contracts. Timestamp and diagnostic helpers remain available even for an empty assembly. Native models and CPU-only Runtime retain the complete public contract for caller-defined providers. Public headers remain available in every profile; unselected physical device operations do not become a second implicit provider. Compilation selection and final ELF garbage collection are measured separately."
msgstr "Physical Platform builds compile the selected controller domains and authored component dependencies from the CMake source contracts. Timestamp and diagnostic helpers remain available even for an empty assembly. Native models and CPU-only Runtime retain the complete public contract for caller-defined providers. Public headers remain available in every profile; unselected physical device operations do not become a second implicit provider. Compilation selection and final ELF garbage collection are measured separately."

msgid "Public component targets declare their own I/O domain dependencies. For example, `Nexus::TMP117I2C` links `Nexus::IOI2C`, so an external owner may supply an endpoint without inventing a physical controller in the assembly. Domain archives are excluded until selected or linked, and shared mechanisms compile once. Optional targets can still appear in `compile_commands.json`; selected Ninja command closures and fresh builds establish which sources actually compile."
msgstr "Public component targets declare their own I/O domain dependencies. For example, `Nexus::TMP117I2C` links `Nexus::IOI2C`, so an external owner may supply an endpoint without inventing a physical controller in the assembly. Domain archives are excluded until selected or linked, and shared mechanisms compile once. Optional targets can still appear in `compile_commands.json`; selected Ninja command closures and fresh builds establish which sources actually compile."

